+    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
+# What it does
+
+3Dtrees: Raster computes fixed-size tile metrics of forest structure (20 m
+tiles by default) from one segmented point cloud. It also writes a digital
+terrain model (DTM), a canopy height model (CHM), a digital surface model
+(DSM), full-resolution voxel point counts (0.5 m voxels by
+default) and provenance records. No points are subsampled, and the input file
+is never modified. The method and every output are described in the
+[tool README](https://github.com/3dTrees-earth/3Dtrees_Raster#readme).
+
+# Input
+
+- **Segmented point cloud**: one full-resolution LAS/LAZ or COPC file with a
+  CRS projected in metres, or no CRS (then the products carry none), and at
+  least one supported tree instance dimension:
+  `PredInstance`, `PredInstance_SAT` (SegmentAnyTree), `PredInstance_FM`
+  (ForestMamba) or `PredInstance_RCT` (RayCloudTools).
+- **Restrict to an area of interest** (default No): select Yes to supply a
+  GeoJSON polygon in the point cloud's XY coordinates. Only whole tiles and
+  voxel columns inside it are reported.
+- **Instance dimensions** (optional): empty processes every one of the
+  dimensions above that the point cloud has. Or name one or more, separated by
+  commas without spaces; the job fails if one is missing from the point cloud.
+- **Remove noise points** (default off): the kNN distance filter flags
+  points whose mean distance to their 8 nearest neighbours exceeds the whole
+  cloud's mean plus two standard deviations. The terrain model, canopy models
+  and tile metrics then use the remaining points.
+- **Advanced parameters**: tile size, voxel sizes, raster resolutions and the
+  tree-acceptance thresholds. Metric voxels and CHM cells must divide 1 m
+  evenly, and DTM cells must divide 60 m. Keep the defaults to stay comparable
+  with other 3Dtrees products.
+
+CPU, memory and scratch space come from the Galaxy job allocation.
+
+# Outputs
+
+Per instance dimension (collections named by dimension):
+
+- **Tile metrics**: one row per tile with vegetation density, height
+  statistics, vertical complexity, canopy roughness and tree statistics.
+- **Segment diagnostics**: one row per segment with the tree-acceptance checks,
+  apex position, crown area and voxel volume.
+- **Tiles**: the tile metrics as GeoJSON polygons.
+
+Shared:
+
+- **DTM**, **CHM** and **DSM** as Cloud Optimized
+  GeoTIFFs (plain GeoTIFF on request), and a PNG tile overview.
+- **Voxel point counts**: occupied voxels as CSV, a multiband UInt32 GeoTIFF
+  (band b holds heights from (b-1)×s to b×s above the DTM for voxel size s), a
+  validity raster (0 excluded, 1 valid, 2 invalid DTM), the same voxels as a
+  COPC point cloud for 3D viewers (an empty dataset when no voxel is
+  occupied), and grid metadata. Counts include every recorded point, also
+  those flagged as noise.
+- **Rejected noise points** and a **Denoising report** (with the filter only).
+- **Run provenance** and **Analysis footprint** records.
